{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "3d45bab4-aef9-507c-b213-348b0614a097"/*VdbFilesExample*/,
  "Description": "A test scene for real-world VDB files. Three level sets from the OpenVDB samples - the armadillo, the buddha and a torus knot - are read with [LoadVdb], made coarser with [VolumeResample] and meshed with [VolumeToMesh]. Balls fall onto the armadillo, whose mesh is their collider.\n\nThe fire is an EmberGen cache of 100 frames, played as a sequence: Path marks the frame number with %d and Frame follows the playback time. EmberGen writes Z-up files in voxel units, so [LoadVdb] turns them upright and scales them as it reads them. Its temperature and flames grids are negated with [VolumeMath], because [NanoVdbRender] reads density from the depth below the zero level, and raymarched together.\n\nEvery file is read and processed on background threads: the scene appears piece by piece while playback keeps running.\n\nThe files are expected in D:\\DEVDEVDEV\\vdbs; change the Path of each [LoadVdb] for another folder.\n\nAKA: vdb files, openvdb samples, embergen, fire sequence, armadillo, buddha\n\nTips\n- The armadillo file holds 22 million voxels: it takes a few seconds to appear, the rest keeps playing.\n- A finer VoxelSize on [VolumeResample] gives a smoother mesh with more triangles.\n- The ground explosion cache plays the same way: point Path at ground_explosion_####.vdb and Mod at 200.",
